{
  "id": "task_007",
  "title": "Weighted Job Scheduling with Cooldown",
  "language": "python",
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "source": "Custom \u2014 weighted job scheduling + cooldown constraint",
  "description": "Write a Python function `max_weight(jobs: list[list[int]], cooldown: int) -> int`.\n\nYou are given a list of jobs where `jobs[i] = [start, end, weight]` (start inclusive, end exclusive). You can select a subset of non-overlapping jobs to maximize total weight, subject to a **cooldown** constraint: after finishing a job that ends at time `e`, the next selected job must start at time >= `e + cooldown`.\n\nReturn the maximum total weight achievable.\n\nFunction signature:\ndef max_weight(jobs: list[list[int]], cooldown: int) -> int:",
  "function_signature": "def max_weight(jobs: list[list[int]], cooldown: int) -> int:",
  "constraints": [
    "0 <= len(jobs) <= 10^4",
    "0 <= start < end <= 10^9",
    "1 <= weight <= 10^4",
    "0 <= cooldown <= 10^9"
  ],
